{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}
<section class="mast">
  <p class="meta"><span class="label en">Weeks 3 &amp; 4 · Sea of Japan side of Hokkaido</span><span class="label ja">3〜4週目・道央日本海側</span><span class="label">Issued {{ d.issued }}</span><span class="label">Valid {{ d.weeks[0].valid[0] }} to {{ d.weeks[1].valid[1] }}</span><span class="label nerd-only">Inits ECMWF {{ d.init_dates.ecmwf }}, JMA {{ d.init_dates.jma }}</span></p>
  <h1>{{ d.headline }}</h1>
  <p class="dek normie-only">{{ site.wording.signal_blurb }}</p>
  <p class="dek nerd-only">Circulation indices from the ECMWF and JMA ensembles, calibrated with Probabilistic Bias Correction, then mapped to a western Hokkaido snow week. The headline number is the lift over the debiased model, with a block-bootstrap interval.</p>
</section>

{% if d.preview %}<p class="note"><span><strong>Design preview.</strong> Every number on this page is fixture data. None of it is a forecast.</span></p>{% endif %}
{% if d.stale %}<p class="note"><span>No new model data since {{ d.stale_since }}. This is the last good outlook. It is ageing.</span></p>{% endif %}
{% if not d.snow_model.skilful %}<p class="note"><span>The snow mapping does not beat climatology in the backtest (RPSS {{ d.snow_model.skill.rpss|num }}, {{ d.snow_model.skill.period }}), so the snow-week calls are greyed. The indices are the product until it does.</span></p>{% endif %}

<section class="weeks" aria-labelledby="weeks-h">
  <h2 id="weeks-h"><span class="en">{{ site.wording.signal_name }}</span><span class="ja">先読みシグナル</span></h2>
  <div class="panels panels-2">
  {% for w in d.weeks %}
    <article class="panel{% if not d.snow_model.skilful %} is-off{% endif %}">
      <div class="panel-head"><span class="label">{{ w.label }}</span><span class="asof">{{ w.valid[0] }} – {{ w.valid[1][5:] }}</span></div>
      <div class="numeral"><span class="numeral-v">{{ pct(w.big_week) }}<span class="numeral-u">%</span></span><span class="numeral-ctx">chance of a big week (top fifth of {{ w.label|lower }}s for the date)</span></div>
      <p class="grade">{{ w.grade }}{% if w.grade != "No signal" %} signal{% endif %}</p>
      <p id="t-{{ w.lead }}" class="sr-only">{{ w.label }}: below normal {{ pct(w.terciles.below) }} percent, near normal {{ pct(w.terciles.near) }} percent, above normal {{ pct(w.terciles.above) }} percent.</p>
      {{ tercile_bar(w.terciles, label_id="t-" ~ w.lead, subject=d.snow_model.skilful and w.grade != "No signal") }}
      <div class="tercile-legend"><span>below</span><span>near normal</span><span>above</span></div>
      <p class="plain">{{ w.line }}</p>
      <div class="nerd-only">
        <p class="rubric-head">What moves the odds (logistic-model term contributions)</p>
        {{ factor_bars(w.factors) }}
        <table class="tbl sr-only"><caption>Factor contributions for {{ w.label }}</caption><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Contribution</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          {% for f in w.factors %}<tr><td>{{ f.name }}</td><td class="r">{{ f.contribution|num('+') }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
        {% if w.lift %}
        <details class="skill"><summary>{{ w.lift_badge }}</summary>
          <p>Lift first. The debiased model scores RPSS <span class="num">{{ w.lift.skill_debiased|num }}</span> and the raw model <span class="num">{{ w.lift.skill_raw|num }}</span> against climatology. The calibrated product scores <span class="num">{{ w.lift.skill_pbc|num }}</span>. The difference to the debiased model, with its 95 % block-bootstrap interval ({{ w.skill.period }}), is the headline. Big-week Brier skill <span class="num">{{ w.skill.bss_big|num }}</span>, ROC area <span class="num">{{ w.skill.roc_big|num }}</span>. At weeks 3 and 4 these numbers are small when they are real.</p></details>
        {% else %}<p class="small muted">No skill shown yet.</p>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </article>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chain" aria-labelledby="chain-h">
  <h2 id="chain-h"><span class="en">Five things in a row</span><span class="ja">雪のレシピ</span></h2>
  <p class="muted">A big week on the Sea of Japan side needs all five. The last column is the model's lean for each week.</p>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th class="normie-only">What</th><th class="nerd-only">Mechanism</th><th class="nerd-only">Indices</th><th>Week 3</th><th>Week 4</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for st in d.weeks[0].stages %}{% set st4 = d.weeks[1].stages[loop.index0] %}{% set idxs = d.indices|selectattr('stage', 'equalto', st.id)|list %}
    <tr><td>{{ loop.index }}. {{ st.name }}</td><td class="normie-only">{{ stage_copy(st.id, 'normie') }}</td><td class="nerd-only">{{ stage_copy(st.id, 'nerd') }}</td><td class="nerd-only">{% for ix in idxs %}{{ ix.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td><td class="state-{{ st.state|replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ st.state }}</td><td class="state-{{ st4.state|replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ st4.state }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section class="research" aria-labelledby="research-h">
  <h2 id="research-h"><span class="en">Built on published work</span><span class="ja">根拠となる研究</span></h2>
  <p>The calibration is Probabilistic Bias Correction{{ cites(("guan2026advancing", "Guan, Mouatadid et al. 2026")) }}, which grew out of adaptive bias correction for subseasonal forecasts{{ cites(("mouatadid2023adaptive", "Mouatadid et al. 2023")) }}. I apply it to the ECMWF and JMA ensembles in the WMO S2S database and verify against ERA5. The ingredient chain is the standard physics of Sea of Japan snow: the Siberian High{{ cites(("panagiotopoulos2005observed", "Panagiotopoulos et al. 2005")) }}, the winter monsoon gradient{{ cites(("hanawa1988surface", "Hanawa et al. 1988"), ("wang2010how", "Wang & Chen 2010")) }}, sea-effect instability over warm water{{ cites(("steenburgh2020perspectives", "Steenburgh & Nakai 2020"), ("west2019characteristics", "West et al. 2019"), ("takahashi2013impact", "Takahashi & Idenaga 2013")) }}, the polar vortex and Arctic Oscillation{{ cites(("thompson1998arctic", "Thompson & Wallace 1998"), ("baldwin2001stratospheric", "Baldwin & Dunkerton 2001"), ("kretschmer2018more", "Kretschmer et al. 2018")) }}, and Ural blocking{{ cites(("peings2019ural", "Peings 2019")) }}. I add no physics. The test is whether calibration beats the model's own debiased output{{ cites(("weigel2007discrete", "Weigel et al. 2007"), ("delsole2014comparing", "DelSole & Tippett 2014")) }}. Full list in Nerd mode and on the <a href="{{ rel }}method.html">method page</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="drivers" aria-labelledby="drivers-h">
  <h2 id="drivers-h"><span class="en">What I can see now</span><span class="ja">現在の背景場</span></h2>
  <div class="panels panels-5">
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><span class="label">Arctic Oscillation</span><span class="asof nerd-only">{{ d.drivers.ao.date }}</span></div><div class="numeral"><span class="numeral-v">{{ d.drivers.ao.value|num('+', 1) }}</span><span class="numeral-ctx">{% if d.drivers.ao.value <= -1 %}negative: cold air spills south{% elif d.drivers.ao.value >= 1 %}positive: cold air stays polar{% else %}near neutral{% endif %}</span></div></div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><span class="label">MJO</span></div>{{ mjo_wheel(d.drivers.mjo.phase, d.drivers.mjo.amp, d.drivers.mjo.rmm1, d.drivers.mjo.rmm2, 88) }}<p class="numeral-ctx">phase {{ d.drivers.mjo.phase }}, amplitude <span class="num">{{ d.drivers.mjo.amp|num('', 1) }}</span>{% if d.drivers.mjo.amp < 1 %} (weak){% endif %}</p></div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><span class="label">Polar vortex</span><span class="asof nerd-only">{{ d.drivers.vortex.date }}</span></div><div class="numeral"><span class="numeral-v">{{ d.drivers.vortex.u10|num('', 0) }}<span class="numeral-u">m/s</span></span><span class="numeral-ctx">{{ d.drivers.vortex.state }}: 10 hPa wind at 60°N</span></div></div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><span class="label">Sea of Japan SST</span></div><div class="numeral"><span class="numeral-v">{{ d.drivers.sst_anom|num('+', 1) }}<span class="numeral-u">°C</span></span><span class="numeral-ctx">{% if d.drivers.sst_anom > 0.3 %}warm sea: more fuel for sea-effect snow{% elif d.drivers.sst_anom < -0.3 %}cool sea: less fuel{% else %}near normal{% endif %}</span></div></div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><span class="label">Recent snow</span></div>
      {% for name, r in d.drivers.recent_snow.items() %}<p class="numeral-ctx"><span class="ja-inline">{{ r.ja }}</span> {{ name }} <span class="num">{{ r.obs_cm }}</span> cm vs <span class="num">{{ r.normal_cm }}</span> cm normal</p>{% endfor %}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="indices nerd-only" aria-labelledby="idx-h">
  <h2 id="idx-h"><span class="en">Index outlooks</span><span class="ja">循環指数の見通し</span></h2>
  <p class="muted">Five equally likely bins after calibration. The dashed line is climatology. A panel with no demonstrated improvement over the debiased model is greyed.</p>
  <div class="panels panels-3">
  {% for ix in d.indices %}
    <article class="panel{% if not (ix.skilful['19'] or ix.skilful['26']) %} is-off{% endif %}">
      <div class="panel-head"><span class="label">{{ ix.name }}</span><span class="asof">stage {{ ix.stage }}</span></div>
      {% for lead in ['19', '26'] %}
      <div class="idx-lead{% if not ix.skilful[lead] %} idx-off{% endif %}">
        <div class="idx-row"><span>Week {{ 3 if lead == '19' else 4 }}</span><span class="num" title="{{ ix.lift_badge[lead] }}">{% if ix.skilful[lead] %}lift {{ ix.skill[lead].lift.lift|num('+') }} · RPSS {{ ix.skill[lead].rpss|num }}{% else %}no demonstrated improvement{% endif %}</span></div>
        {{ quintile_bar(ix.quintiles[lead], subject=ix.skilful[lead]) }}
        <p class="plain small">{{ ix.line[lead] }}</p>
        <table class="tbl sr-only"><caption>{{ ix.name }} week {{ 3 if lead == '19' else 4 }} quintile probabilities</caption><tbody><tr>{% for p in ix.quintiles[lead] %}<td>{{ pct(p) }}%</td>{% endfor %}</tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <details><summary>Definition</summary><p class="small">{{ index_help(ix.key) }}</p>
        <p class="small muted">Lift is the calibrated RPSS minus the debiased model's RPSS, with a 95 % block-bootstrap interval. Week 3: {{ ix.lift_badge['19'] }}. Week 4: {{ ix.lift_badge['26'] }}.</p></details>
    </article>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="maps nerd-only" aria-labelledby="maps-h">
  <h2 id="maps-h"><span class="en">Maps</span><span class="ja">地図</span></h2>
  <details><summary>Show the week-3 maps (most-likely quintile, shaded by confidence)</summary>
    <div class="map-grid">
    {% for m in d.maps %}
      <figure><figcaption class="label">{{ m.title }} · week 3</figcaption><img src="{{ rel }}{{ m.file }}" alt="{{ m.title }} week-3 map: most likely quintile per 1.5-degree cell, shaded by confidence" loading="lazy" width="640" height="400"></figure>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">Dashed boxes are the index regions. The solid box is Hokkaido. 1.5° grid, 21–72°N, 75°E–135°W.</p>
  </details>
</section>

<section class="season nerd-only" aria-labelledby="season-h">
  <h2 id="season-h"><span class="en">Season so far</span><span class="ja">シーズンの推移</span></h2>
  <figure class="fig"><span class="label">Fig. 1</span><figcaption id="season-desc" class="fig-title">Observed weekly snow against climatology, with the tercile I called 3 (▲) and 4 (△) weeks earlier</figcaption>
  {{ season_chart(d.season) }}
  <p class="fig-src">ERA5 snowfall over western Hokkaido, mm water equivalent, weekly. Grey band: 20th to 80th percentile of the 20-year climatology. The calls stay on the chart whether or not they verified.</p></figure>
  <details><summary>Data table</summary><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Week start</th><th class="r">Observed</th><th class="r">Clim 20–80 %</th><th>Called at wk3</th><th>Called at wk4</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for w in d.season %}<tr><td class="num">{{ w.start }}</td><td class="r">{{ w.obs }}</td><td class="r">{{ w.clim_lo }}–{{ w.clim_hi }}</td><td>{{ w.fc19 }}</td><td>{{ w.fc26 }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></details>
</section>

<section class="nerd nerd-only" aria-labelledby="nerd-h">
  <h2 id="nerd-h"><span class="en">Results, method, limits</span><span class="ja">結果・手法・限界</span></h2>
  <p class="muted">{{ d.backtest.note }}</p>
  <h3>Lift over the model is the headline number</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Target</th><th class="r">Model skill (debiased RPSS)</th><th class="r">PBC lift</th><th class="r">95 % CI</th><th class="r">Stage-3 lift</th><th class="r">95 % CI</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for r in d.backtest.lift %}<tr><td>{{ r.what }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.model_skill|num }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.pbc_lift|num('+') }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.pbc_ci[0]|num('+') }} to {{ r.pbc_ci[1]|num('+') }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.stage3_lift|num('+') }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.stage3_ci[0]|num('+') }} to {{ r.stage3_ci[1]|num('+') }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
  <p class="note"><span>Three layers, kept apart: what the dynamical model already knew, what PBC adds, what the ingredient model adds. An interval that spans zero reads "no demonstrated improvement".</span></p>
  <h3>Index lift by lead</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Index</th><th>Stage</th><th class="r">Week 3 lift (CI)</th><th class="r">Week 3 RPSS</th><th class="r">Week 4 lift (CI)</th><th class="r">Week 4 RPSS</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for ix in d.indices %}<tr><td>{{ ix.name }}</td><td>{{ ix.stage }}</td>{% for lead in ['19', '26'] %}{% set sk = ix.skill[lead] %}{% if sk and sk.lift %}<td class="r">{{ sk.lift.lift|num('+') }} ({{ sk.lift.ci[0]|num('+') }}, {{ sk.lift.ci[1]|num('+') }})</td><td class="r">{{ sk.rpss|num }}</td>{% else %}<td class="r">not scored</td><td class="r">–</td>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Windows of opportunity</h3>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Condition at issue time</th><th class="r">n weeks</th><th class="r">Snow-week RPSS</th><th class="r">95 % CI</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for r in d.backtest.windows %}<tr><td>{{ r.condition }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.n }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.rpss|num }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.ci[0]|num('+') }} to {{ r.ci[1]|num('+') }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Sample size and experiments</h3>
  <p><span class="num">{{ d.backtest.effective_n.weeks }}</span> DJF weeks in the open test winters. Effective sample about <span class="num">{{ d.backtest.effective_n.effective }}</span> after autocorrelation. Experiment log: <span class="num">{{ d.backtest.experiments.n_trials }}</span> configurations evaluated{% if d.backtest.experiments.best is not none %}; best <span class="num">{{ d.backtest.experiments.best|num }}</span>, deflated for selection <span class="num">{{ d.backtest.experiments.deflated|num }}</span>{% endif %}. The last three winters (2023/24 to 2025/26) are sealed. {% if d.backtest.final_exam %}I evaluated them once: {{ d.backtest.final_exam }}{% else %}I have not evaluated them yet{% endif %}.</p>
  <h3>Limits</h3>
  <ul class="small">
    <li>About ten winters of 13 DJF weeks each, autocorrelated. Intervals are wide. A non-significant lift reads as no signal.</li>
    <li>1.5° fields cannot resolve Hokkaido's terrain or the JPCZ. Delivery (stage 5) is explained, not forecast.</li>
    <li>ERA5 snowfall is biased in mountains. SNOW-W is a box average checked against AMeDAS stations, not a resort total.</li>
    <li>JMA changed system several times in the period and its ensembles are small. ECMWF changed cycle in 2023, 2024 and 2026.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Reproducibility</h3>
  <p class="small">Commit <code>{{ d.repro.commit }}</code>, state version <code>{{ d.repro.state_version }}</code>. One command: <code>{{ d.repro.command }}</code>. Method in full: <a href="{{ rel }}method.html">method page</a>, <code>docs/METHOD.md</code>, <code>docs/BACKTEST.md</code>.</p>
  <h3>References</h3>
  {% if d.references %}<ol class="refs">{% for r in d.references %}<li id="ref-{{ r.key }}">{{ r.text }}{% if r.doi %} <a href="https://doi.org/{{ r.doi }}">doi:{{ r.doi }}</a>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>
  {% else %}<p class="small muted">The reference list is built from <code>references.bib</code> once every entry has passed the checks in <code>docs/REFERENCES_CHECK.md</code>. An unverified reference never appears here.</p>{% endif %}
</section>
{% endblock %}
